description:
This is a bite-sized session to give health and care professionals an overview of vulnerabilities across the life course - including key evidence, data and signposting to trusted resources to help prevent illness, protect health and promote wellbeing.
Vulnerabilities, risk factor, protective factor, vulnerable background, trauma, trauma-informed practice, support
&nbsp;

A brief introduction to Inclusion Health
Inclusion Health aims to prevent and redress unequal health outcomes for people from disadvantaged populations, including people experiencing homelessness, sex workers, vulnerable migrants and Gypsies and Travellers.
&nbsp;
